{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"supersampling","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Supersampling provides increased lightmap quality with less noise, smoother shadows and better shadowing of small-scale features in objects. However, it may result in significantly increased bake times and memory usage while baking lightmaps. Padding is automatically adjusted to avoid increasing light leaking."}]}]}],"metadata":{"title":"supersampling","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot10LightmapGIC13supersamplingSbvp","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"supersampling"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/lightmapgi\/supersampling"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/LightmapGI\/supersampling","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/LightmapGI"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", lightmaps are baked with the texel scale multiplied with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/LightmapGI\/supersamplingFactor"},{"type":"text","text":" and downsampled before saving the lightmap (so the effective texel density is identical to having supersampling disabled)."}],"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Framework to write Godot Game Extensions using the Swift Programming Language."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","title":"SwiftGodot","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/LightmapGI/supersamplingFactor":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"supersamplingFactor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/lightmapgi\/supersamplingfactor","kind":"symbol","title":"supersamplingFactor","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The factor by which the texel density is multiplied for supersampling. For best results, use an integer value. While fractional values are allowed, they can result in increased light leaking and a blurry lightmap."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/LightmapGI\/supersamplingFactor"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/LightmapGI/supersampling":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", lightmaps are baked with the texel scale multiplied with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/LightmapGI\/supersamplingFactor","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and downsampled before saving the lightmap (so the effective texel density is identical to having supersampling disabled)."}],"type":"topic","rol